{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% from "_macros.j2" import todo, mailto, places %}
{% block title %}{{ b.brand }}: {{ b.tagline }}{% endblock %}
{% block main %}
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">For CQC compliance consultancies</p>
    <h1>Know which care services need CQC help, the week it happens.</h1>
    <p class="lead">Every Monday, {{ b.brand }} sends you the care providers in your area that have just been rated
      poorly, just registered with CQC, just become due for an inspection, or just been set up as a company. It comes
      with contact details and the rules for contacting each one.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      {% if b.email %}<a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:{{ b.email }}?subject={{ 'Free trial' | urlencode }}">Start a free trial</a>{% endif %}
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="sample.html">See a sample</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% if d.has_numbers %}
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Live from the registers</p>
    <h2>{{ d.region_name }}, the last {{ d.weeks | length }} weeks</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">{{ d.period }}. Counted from the official CQC and Companies House registers.</p>
    <div class="stats">
    {% for value, label, note in d.stats() %}
      <div class="stat"><div class="v">{{ value }}</div><div class="l">{{ label }}</div><div class="n">{{ note }}</div></div>
    {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="stats-note"><a href="sample.html">See anonymised examples</a></p>
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<section id="what">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">What you get</p>
    <h2>Five lists of warm leads, every week</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Each lead appears once, in the week it happens, so you're first to know and never see
      the same name twice.</p>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">Highest intent</span><h3>New poor ratings</h3>
        <p>Services just rated Requires improvement or Inadequate, with their previous rating. They need an action plan
          before CQC comes back.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">First inspection due</span><h3>Newly registered services</h3>
        <p>Care services that have just registered with CQC and have never been inspected. Their first inspection is on
          its way.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">Inspection coming</span><h3>Due for inspection</h3>
        <p>Services whose rating is 4 or more years old, or that have waited a year for a first inspection. CQC is
          working through these first: the moment for a mock inspection. You also get the full list for your area.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">Earliest possible</span><h3>New care companies</h3>
        <p>Companies just set up to provide care, most of which still need to register with CQC. We flag which are
          already registered.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="tag">Found for you</span><h3>Companies now located</h3>
        <p>New companies that used a formation agent's address are watched until they reveal where they operate, then
          passed to you.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
    <h2>No searching, no spreadsheets to build</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><h3>Choose your area</h3><p>A CQC region, a list of councils, or postcode areas. Cover as many
        as you work in.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><h3>We watch the registers</h3><p>CQC and Companies House are checked every week for new
        ratings, registrations and companies in your area.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><h3>You get the digest</h3><p>An easy-to-read page and spreadsheets that open in Excel, with
        phone, website and links to the official records.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Compliant by design</p>
    <h2>Built for UK GDPR and PECR</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card"><h3>Contact rule on every lead</h3><p>Each lead is labelled "email OK", "phone (check TPS/CTPS
        first)" or "post only" from its legal form, so you stay on the right side of PECR.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>No personal names collected</h3><p>Registered managers' and nominated individuals' names are
        removed before anything is stored.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Opt-outs honoured</h3><p>Anyone who asks is removed and never listed again. See our
        <a href="privacy.html">privacy notice</a>.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="pricing">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
    <h2>One simple price per area</h2>
    <div class="pricing">
      <div class="price-card">
        {% if b.price_per_region %}
        <div class="price">£{{ "%g" | format(b.price_per_region) }} <small>{{ b.price_note }}</small></div>
        {% else %}
        <div class="price">{{ todo("set price_per_region in business.yaml") }}</div>
        {% endif %}
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>Weekly digest every Monday</li>
          <li>All five lead lists, plus the full never-inspected and due-for-inspection lists for your area</li>
          <li>Independents first: services run by large groups, which have their own quality teams, are left out</li>
          <li>Spreadsheets that open in Excel</li>
          <li>Contact rule on every lead</li>
          <li>National list of new care companies with unknown locations</li>
        </ul>
        {% if b.places_per_area %}<p>{{ places(b) }}</p>{% endif %}
        {% if b.exclusive_price %}<p>Want your area to yourself? <strong>£{{ "%g" | format(b.exclusive_price) }} a
          month</strong> and no other consultancy gets your leads.</p>{% endif %}
        {% if b.trial %}<p><strong>{{ b.trial }}</strong></p>{% endif %}
        {% if b.email %}<a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:{{ b.email }}?subject={{ 'Free trial' | urlencode }}">Start a free trial</a>{% endif %}
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Is it worth it?</h3>
        <p>One new client can pay for many months of leads. Poor ratings, first inspections and brand-new
          providers are the moments care services look for help, and this puts you in front of them first.</p>
        {% if b.places_per_area %}
        <h3>Why a limit per area?</h3>
        <p>A lead is worth most when you're one of very few people calling. We sell each area to at most
          {{ b.places_per_area }} {{ "consultancy" if b.places_per_area == 1 else "consultancies" }}{% if b.exclusive_price %}, or to
          just you on the exclusive plan{% endif %}.</p>
        {% endif %}
        <h3>Which areas?</h3>
        <p>Anywhere in England: London, a whole CQC region, a group of councils, or just the postcodes around your
          office.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="faq">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <details><summary>Where does the information come from?</summary>
      <p>From the official public registers: the Care Quality Commission's API and Companies House. We add value by
        spotting the changes that matter each week, linking companies to their CQC registrations, and working out the
        legal form and contact rule for each lead.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is this legal under GDPR and PECR?</summary>
      <p>The leads are organisations, from registers published for transparency. We remove the names of registered
        managers and nominated individuals, label every lead with the PECR contact rule, and honour opt-outs. Some
        providers are sole traders: treat their details as personal data, contact them only about relevant services,
        and stop if asked.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Couldn't I just search the CQC website?</summary>
      <p>You could, every week, for every service in your area, and compare the results with last week's. We do that
        for you, add new companies from Companies House, and follow up companies registered at formation agents until
        they show where they operate.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Will other consultancies get the same leads?</summary>
      <p>{% if b.places_per_area %}Very few. {{ places(b) }}{% if b.exclusive_price %} On the exclusive plan
        (£{{ "%g" | format(b.exclusive_price) }} a month), nobody else gets your area's leads.{% endif %}{% else %}Each
        area is open to any number of subscribers.{% endif %}</p></details>
    <details><summary>Do you include the big care groups?</summary>
      <p>Not by default. Services run by large groups (CQC lists them under a brand, or they have 10 or more locations)
        have in-house quality teams and rarely hire consultants, so we leave them out. Every lead is labelled
        "independent" or "multi-site". Tell us if you want the groups included.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What format is it in?</summary>
      <p>A web page you can open, print or forward, and CSV spreadsheets for Excel, Numbers or your CRM.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I cancel?</summary>
      <p>Yes, any time. There's no minimum term.</p></details>
    <p style="margin-top:24px">Anything else? {{ mailto(b, "Question about " ~ b.brand, "Email us") }}.</p>
  </div>
</section>
{% endblock %}
